    "AI Notes": {
      "value": "London-based still-life photographer, BA Photography at Falmouth University. Conceptual still life exploring colour, tone and form via playful arrangements of everyday objects (from Poundland finds to designer objects). Named projects: Pound Series (letters spelled in composed everyday objects), Simple Constructions (inspired by a 1972 book), Waves (book collaboration with Jake Kenny, 2021), Two Times Twice (with set designer Saskia Martindale). Editorial and commercial clients: FT How to Spend It, FT Weekend, Wallpaper, WeTransfer WePresent, Evening Standard Magazine, Refinery29 x Amex, Port, Soho House Magazine, Dr Martens, Esquire. Senior-level freelance: solo commercial practice, handles own shoots, no employer listed anywhere. Autonomy 4: runs own commissions independently. Work captured from Wallpaper* (2018 profile), Its Nice That (2019 feature, Pound Series + Simple Constructions), Loupe Magazine (2022, Waves book). Website (andyprice.co, Squarespace) expired at time of scrape. IG @__andyprice__ blocked logged-out (headless Playwright returns error page); queued to ig-queue.json for logged-in grab. LinkedIn and email confirmed present.",
